If the dot is identified with $x$, then we get the third picture. However, Lemma \ref{cycle} can be applied neither to the inside nor to the outside of the thick simple closed path, because either side contains a vertex of degree $>3$ in the interior. To resolve the problem, we may either change the simple closed path to the one in the fourth picture and apply Lemma \ref{cycle} to the outside, or we may modify the simple closed path in the third picture to the one in the fifth picture and apply Lemma \ref{cycle}.

With suitable choice of the sequence of constructing tiles and extra care, we can indeed show that, starting from any meridian, the developments to the right side must be generic.

