Now we deal with the third thing. We start with any meridian and add successive timezones. As long as we have at least two edges available at each pole, we may continue adding timezone. If there are exactly two edges available at each poles, then we can complete the final timezone and get the earth map tiling. This fails exactly when we have no or one edge left in one pole and at least one edge left at the other pole. Figure \ref{special2} describes the failing cases for the meridian $[3]$. Applying Lemma \ref{cycle}, these failing cases cannot happen. The same reason applies to the other meridians.
\end{proof}





