1964:By Figure \ref{impossible}, (3.1) and (4.1) are impossible. By considering the outside of the configurations, (3.2) and (4.4) are also impossible. Moreover, applying Lemma \ref{sequence} to $(6.3)$ gives $(3.1)$, which we have shown is impossible. Applying the lemma to the outside of $(6.2)$ gives similar contradiction. We conclude that the configurations $(3.1)$, $(3.2)$, $(4.1)$, $(4.4)$, $(6.2)$, $(6.3)$ are all impossible. For the remaining configurations, we follow the argument in the proof of Lemma \ref{cycle}. All the non-generic reductions can be dismissed as before, so that we only need to consider the generic reductions in Figure \ref{xyz_reduce}. A subtle point in constructing the reductions is to make sure that all the newly created vertices are of distance $\le 3$ from the high degree boundary vertex, so that the new vertices have degree $3$.
