2480:\begin{proof}
2481:Theorem \ref{distance5} covers the case that the distances between vertices of degree $>3$ are always $\ge 5$. Moreover, under the assumption of the current theorem, the whole proof of Theorem \ref{distance5} except the last paragraph is still valid. We may still conclude that $x_*,y_*,z_*$ are all distinct, and $w_*$ is not identified with any of $x_*,y_*,z_*$. In fact, if we also know that all $w_*$ are distinct, then the tiling must be the earth map tiling in Figure \ref{map5}.
